seg-1524fb5b0aba = Principles

# text
seg-82b8ed15bbe6 = Receive is the product, and transmitting is never in the open code.

# text
seg-63c000eccfc2 = Every hardware session yields an evidence pack with hashes of the inputs, the conditions and the thresholds used.

# text
seg-63cc5d9513ff = A conducted or shielded attestation is recorded, never inferred.

# text
seg-da1e4f5da956 = Numbers that come from hardware stay <b>MODELLED</b> until an independent external oracle agrees (for example a laboratory truth trajectory or a reference clock). A pre-registered bar is not loosened after a run.

# text
seg-d8e445427d02 = Antennas with controlled patterns, inertial units and chip-scale atomic clocks are treated as data sources (patterns, logs, published stability curves), not as devices Kshana drives.

# text
seg-7a22a9591fa3 = Wording: a result is "measured against the mask" or "supports evidence for" a requirement. Kshana does not say that a device meets a standard, and nobody has rated or approved it.

# text
seg-913509e5d6b2 = Legal notes (owner legal review pending)

# text
seg-c18b68936406 = Receiving GNSS signals is legal almost everywhere. Transmitting in GNSS bands is not.

# text
seg-070d8a8d5494 = <b>United States.</b> Wilful interference with radio communications is barred under { "47" } U.S.C. §{ "333" }, and the FCC enforces against jammers (<a1>https://www.fcc.gov/general/jammer-enforcement</a1>). A transmission from a bench can reach beyond the bench.

# text
seg-336b48c6f5f2 = <b>Elsewhere.</b> The maintainers have not reviewed other countries' law. The community around gps-sdr-sim states that transmitting its output is prohibited by law in most countries; treat that as the working assumption wherever counsel has not said otherwise.

# text
seg-8d31cbd38718 = <b>A shielded or conducted setup is a safeguard, not a licence.</b> The attestation below records the safeguard the operator says was in place. It does not make an emission lawful.

# text
# c1: iq monitor --follow
seg-7373bfd21035 = <b>Recording.</b> Recording radio signals can raise privacy and legality questions in some places. <c1/> and any capture recipe are receive-only, and the operator is responsible for where and what they record.

# text
seg-2edf9b14e62c = <b>Export control.</b> Hardware-in-the-loop software that drives signal generators can fall under export-control rules. That is why stage { "3" } is outside the open engine.

# text
seg-bcd59f201022 = <b>Nothing here is an endorsement or an agreement.</b> No regulator, test range, laboratory or vendor has been consulted about this document or has agreed to anything in it.

